  "final_answer": "## Latest MacBook Model — Apple.com Findings\n\nBased on my research of apple.com, I found information on **two notable MacBook models** that are currently featured:\n\n### 🆕 MacBook Neo (Newest MacBook Line)\nThis is the newest addition to the MacBook family, positioned as an entry-level option. Source: https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/\n\n- **Model Name:** MacBook Neo 13-inch\n- **Processor:** Apple A18 Pro chip\n  - 6-core CPU (2 performance cores + 4 efficiency cores)\n  - 5-core GPU with hardware-accelerated ray tracing\n  - 16-core Neural Engine\n  - 60GB/s memory bandwidth\n  - Media Engine with hardware-accelerated H.264, HEVC, ProRes, and ProRes RAW\n- **Memory:** 8GB unified memory\n- **Storage:** 256GB SSD or 512GB SSD\n- **Display:** 13.0-inch Liquid Retina display (2408-by-1506 native resolution at 219 pixels per inch, 500 nits brightness)\n- **Finishes:** Silver, Blush, Citrus, Indigo\n- **Pricing:** Starts at $699 (or $599 with education savings)\n\n### 💻 MacBook Pro (Latest Flagship)\nThe flagship MacBook has been updated with the new M5 family of chips. Source: https://www.apple.com/macbook-pro/\n\n- **Processor Options:** M5, M5 Pro, or M5 Max\n- **Pricing:** Starting at $1,999\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** If interpreting \"latest MacBook model\" as the newest MacBook line introduced, it is the **MacBook Neo with A18 Pro chip, 8GB unified memory, and 256GB/512GB SSD storage**. If interpreting as the latest MacBook flagship, it is the **MacBook Pro with the new M5/M5 Pro/M5 Max chip family**.",
